[38;5;231m⏺[39m I stopped before editing — this one crosses an API boundary.

  [38;5;153mroutes/users.js:6[39m is the [38;5;153mGET /users[39m response shape. Renaming [38;5;153muserId[39m → [38;5;153muser_id[39m there is a breaking change for every
  existing client, and the repo's own README (lines 3-5) names them and states the policy:

  [2m▎[0m [3mConsumers of [38;5;153mGET /users[39m: the web app, the iOS app (3.2 and later), and the nightly partner export. Field names in [0m
  [2m▎[0m [3mthe response are part of the contract; changes go through a versioned endpoint.[0m

  So the "just the field name" change is exactly the thing the README says must go through a version. The iOS app is the
  sharp edge: shipped 3.2+ binaries can't be updated in lockstep, and the nightly partner export is out of your control
  entirely. An in-place rename breaks all three the moment it deploys.

